doc:state_action_enforcementjudge_20161215 a echr:DomesticProceeding ;
    rdfs:label "Belgian State proceedings before the enforcement judge at the Brussels Dutch‑language TPI (15 December 2016)"@en ;
    echr:hasCourt doc:enforcementJudgeBrusselsDutchTpi ;
    echr:hasParticipation doc:participation_applicants_responding_enforcement_20161215,
        doc:participation_state_enforcement_20161215 ;
    echr:hasProceedingStartDate "2016-12-15"^^xsd:date ;
    echr:hasSupportingQuote "On the same date the Belgian State brought proceedings against the applicants before the enforcement judge at the Brussels Dutch ‑ language TPI, seeking a stay of execution of the principal sentence ( condamnation principale ) resulting from the Aliens Appeals Boards’ judgment of 20 October 2016 (obligation to issue visas or laissez ‑ passers ) and/or a stay of execution of the court of appeal’s judgment of 7 December 2016, and/or to prevent other enforcement measures, such as penalty payments."@en .

doc:tpi_inter_partes_2016_11_07 a echr:DomesticProceeding ;
    rdfs:label "Decision by a judge acting as president of the French-language TPI (7 November 2016)"@en ;
    echr:followsProceeding doc:tpi_order_2016_10_25 ;
    echr:hasCourt doc:brusselsTpi ;
    echr:hasDecisionDate "2016-11-07"^^xsd:date ;
    echr:hasParticipation doc:part_tpi_2016_11_07_applicants,
        doc:part_tpi_2016_11_07_belgian_state ;
    echr:hasSupportingQuote "On 7 November 2016 another judge acting as president of the French ‑ language TPI declared their application admissible but unfounded, considering that the Belgian authorities could not be criticised for failing voluntarily to comply with a judgment by the Aliens Appeals Board..."^^xsd:string .

doc:tpi_order_2016_10_25 a echr:DomesticProceeding ;
    rdfs:label "Order by the acting president of the Brussels French-language TPI (25 October 2016)"@en ;
    echr:followsProceeding doc:aliens_appeals_2016_10_20 ;
    echr:hasCourt doc:brusselsTpi ;
    echr:hasDecisionDate "2016-10-25"^^xsd:date ;
    echr:hasParticipation doc:part_tpi_2016_10_25_applicants,
        doc:part_tpi_2016_10_25_belgian_state ;
    echr:hasSupportingQuote "By an order of 25 October 2016, considering that the failure by the Aliens Office to comply with a judgment of the Aliens Appeals Board, notwithstanding the fact that it had been immediately enforceable, constituted “an unacceptable illegal action”, the acting president of the French-language TPI ordered the State, as an urgent measure, to comply with the Board’s judgment of 20 October 2016, that is, to issue the applicants with visas or laissez-passers , and made the order subject to a penalty payment of 1,000 euros (EUR) per day of delay and per applicant."@en .

doc:administrative_action_aliens_refusal_2016_09_13 a echr:AdministrativeAction ;
    rdfs:label "Aliens Office refusal to grant \"humanitarian visas\" (13 September 2016)"@en ;
    echr:hasCourt doc:aliensOffice ;
    echr:hasDecisionDate "2016-09-13"^^xsd:date ;
    echr:hasParticipation doc:part_admin_2016_09_13_aliens_office ;
    echr:hasSupportingQuote "On 13 September 2016 the Aliens Office, the administrative body responsible for issuing visas (see paragraph 45 below), refused to grant “humanitarian visas” to the applicants and informed them of its decisions by an email of 29 September 2016, transmitted through the visa department of the Belgian embassy in Beirut."@en .

doc:aliens_appeals_2017_03_24 a echr:DomesticProceeding ;
    rdfs:label "Aliens Appeals Board judgment dismissing application to set aside (24 March 2017)"@en ;
    echr:followsProceeding doc:aliens_appeals_2016_10_20 ;
    echr:hasCourt doc:aliensAppealsBoard ;
    echr:hasDecisionDate "2017-03-24"^^xsd:date ;
    echr:hasParticipation doc:part_aliens_appeals_2017_03_24_aliens_office,
        doc:part_aliens_appeals_2017_03_24_applicants ;
    echr:hasSupportingQuote "On 24 March 2017 the Aliens Appeals Board dismissed the application to have those decisions set aside, finding that the Aliens Office’s decisions of 13 September 2016 (see paragraph 11 above) had become final and that, in consequence, the applicants no longer had standing to challenge the subsequent decisions."@en .

